---

<Layout
  theme="lab"
  title="Loneliness Strategy, Measurement & Pilot Design | Dr. Axel Schumacher"
  description="Advisory for governments, health bodies, universities, employers and sports clubs: measure the social structures behind the loneliness pandemic, design targeted interventions, and evaluate pilots honestly."
>
  {/* ===== HERO ===== */}
  <section class="hero-org glow-top relative overflow-hidden border-b border-[color:var(--border)]">
    <div class="hero-photo" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="container-x relative z-10 py-24 md:py-28">
      <span class="eyebrow">For governments, institutions & clubs</span>
      <h1 class="mt-6 max-w-4xl text-[clamp(2.2rem,5vw,3.6rem)] font-bold">
        Loneliness is now a global health emergency. You cannot solve what you cannot see.
      </h1>
      <p class="lead mt-7 max-w-xl text-lg">
        In June 2025 the World Health Organization put a number on it: one in six people worldwide,
        and 871,000 deaths a year. The mandate now exists. The method mostly does not. I work with
        institutions on the part that has been missing — turning loneliness from a feeling people
        report into a structure you can see, target, and solve.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-9 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
        <a href="#enquiry" class="btn btn-primary">Discuss a pilot</a>
        <a href="#scale" class="btn btn-ghost">See the evidence</a>
      </div>
      <div class="pill-row">
        <span class="pill">Ph.D. human genetics</span>
        <span class="pill">30+ years in clinical research environments</span>
        <span class="pill">Published sociogram methodology</span>
        <span class="pill">Author, <em>Ending Loneliness</em></span>
        <span class="pill">Munich · EU-based</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* ===== THE SCALE ===== */}
  <section id="scale" class="section">
    <div class="container-x">
      <div class="max-w-2xl">
        <span class="eyebrow">The scale</span>
        <h2 class="mt-5 text-3xl font-semibold md:text-4xl">
          Loneliness kills more people than HIV. Or malaria. Or drugs.
        </h2>
        <p class="lead mt-6">
          Each of those has a dedicated global fund, a UN agency, and national programmes financed in
          the billions. Loneliness kills more people than any of them and has a commission and a
          report.
        </p>
      </div>

      <figure
        class="reveal mt-12 rounded-2xl border border-[color:var(--border)] bg-[color:var(--surface)] p-5 md:p-8"
      >
        <div class="mort-head" aria-hidden="true">
          <span>Cause</span>
          <span>Estimated deaths per year</span>
          <span>Dedicated global financing</span>
        </div>

        <ul class="mort-list">
          {
            mortality.map((m) => (
              <li class={m.hl ? "mort-row is-hl" : "mort-row"}>
                <div class="mort-name">
                  {m.name}
                  <span class="mort-year">{m.year}</span>
                </div>
                <div class="mort-track">
                  <div class="mort-barwrap">
                    <div class="mort-bar" style={`width:${m.pct}%`} />
                  </div>
                  <span class="mort-value">{m.label}</span>
                </div>
                <div class="mort-fund">{m.fund}</div>
              </li>
            ))
          }
        </ul>

        <figcaption
          class="mt-6 border-t border-[color:var(--border)] pt-4 text-xs leading-relaxed text-[color:var(--text-dim)]"
        >
          Estimated deaths per year. Sources: WHO Commission on Social Connection, <em
            >From Loneliness to Social Connection</em
          >, 30 June 2025; UNAIDS fact sheet 2025 (2024 data); WHO World Malaria Report 2025 (2024
          data); WHO global status report on alcohol and drug use (2019 data — the most recent
          comparable global estimate for deaths attributable to psychoactive drug use). Note the
          methods differ: the loneliness figure is an attributable-risk estimate derived from
          association studies, not a cause-of-death code on a certificate. It should be read as an
          order of magnitude, not a body count.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>

      <div class="note-box">
        <h3>Why this is not simply a mental-health problem</h3>
        <p>
          The mortality signal does not run mainly through suicide. It runs through cardiovascular
          disease, stroke, type 2 diabetes, immune function and dementia — which is why House and
          colleagues concluded, as far back as 1988, that social relationships constitute a risk
          factor rivalling smoking, blood pressure and obesity. Loneliness belongs on a health
          ministry's balance sheet, not only in its mental-health directorate.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* ===== QUOTE: NORMAN COUSINS ===== */}
  <section class="photo-band">
    <div class="container-x">
      <div class="quote-layout">
        <div class="quote-panel reveal">
          <span class="eyebrow">The human case</span>
          <blockquote>
            “The eternal quest of the individual human being is to shatter his loneliness.”
          </blockquote>
          <p class="attrib">
            Norman Cousins (1915–1990) — American journalist, author and peace advocate; editor of
            the <em>Saturday Review</em> for three decades.
          </p>
        </div>

        {/* reveal sits on a wrapper: .reveal.is-visible sets transform:none,
            which would otherwise cancel the tilt-card's rotation */}
        <div class="portrait-wrap reveal">
          <figure class="tilt-card portrait-hist">
            <img
              src="/images/photos/norman-cousins.webp"
              alt="Portrait of Norman Cousins"
              width="300"
              height="399"
              loading="lazy"
            />
          </figure>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p
        class="relative z-[1] mx-auto mt-12 max-w-2xl text-center leading-relaxed text-[color:var(--text-muted)]"
      >
        Cousins wrote that decades before the mortality data existed. The quest is not new — what is
        new is that the structures behind it can now be measured, targeted and evaluated.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* ===== MEASUREMENT GAP ===== */}
  <section class="section border-t border-[color:var(--border)]">
    <div class="container-x grid gap-12 md:grid-cols-[0.85fr_1.15fr]">
      <div class="reveal">
        <span class="eyebrow">The measurement gap</span>
        <h2 class="mt-5 text-3xl font-semibold md:text-4xl">
          Most loneliness programs cannot tell whether they worked.
        </h2>
      </div>
      <div class="reveal space-y-5 leading-relaxed text-[color:var(--text-muted)]">
        <p>
          Self-reported loneliness scales tell you how a population feels. They do not tell you which
          structural conditions produced that feeling, which of them a program can change, or whether
          a given intervention changed them. That gap is why well-funded initiatives so often end
          without a defensible answer about impact.
        </p>
        <p>
          My work applies network methods — sociograms and structural indicators — to make the social
          architecture of a population legible: where repeated contact exists, where ties are
          concentrated or absent, and where bridges between groups are missing. That gives a program
          something concrete to target and a baseline against which to evaluate.
        </p>
        <p class="text-[color:var(--text)]">
          Eight years after the first minister for loneliness was appointed, not one country can show
          a population whose loneliness measurably fell and stayed down. The world does not need
          another awareness campaign — it needs a different class of intervention, built to be
          tested.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* ===== DOWNSTREAM: FERTILITY ===== */}
  <section id="fertility" class="section border-t border-[color:var(--border)]">
    <div class="container-x">
      <div class="max-w-2xl">
        <span class="eyebrow">Downstream consequence</span>
        <h2 class="mt-5 text-3xl font-semibold md:text-4xl">A demographic disaster.</h2>
        <p class="lead mt-6">
          We treat falling fertility as an economic problem with an economic fix — tax credits,
          subsidised daycare, paternal leave. It doesn't work. The birth-rate collapse isn't a
          financial calculation; it is a relational breakdown. It is what happens when human
          partnerships stop forming.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-[color:var(--text-muted)]">
          Every line below crosses the replacement threshold — 2.1 births per woman — and never
          recovers.
        </p>
      </div>

      <figure
        class="reveal mx-auto mt-12 max-w-4xl rounded-2xl border border-[color:var(--border)] bg-[color:var(--surface)] p-4 md:p-7"
      >
        <svg
          viewBox="0 0 940 382"
          role="img"
          aria-label="Line chart of total fertility rate from 1960 to 2024 for six Western countries and four East Asian countries and territories. All fall below the replacement rate of 2.1 births per woman and none recovers. By 2024 South Korea is at 0.75, Hong Kong 0.84, Singapore 0.97, Spain 1.10, Japan 1.15, Italy 1.18, Germany 1.36, the United Kingdom 1.55, France 1.61 and the United States 1.63."
          class="h-auto w-full"
        >
          <defs>
            <linearGradient id="subrep" x1="0" y1="0" x2="0" y2="1">
              <stop offset="0%" stop-color="var(--accent)" stop-opacity="0.13" />
              <stop offset="100%" stop-color="var(--accent)" stop-opacity="0" />
            </linearGradient>
          </defs>

          {/* grid */}
          {
            yTicks.map((t) => (
              <line x1="86" x2="880" y1={t.y} y2={t.y} stroke="var(--border)" stroke-width="1" />
            ))
          }

          {/* sub-replacement zone */}
          <rect x="86" y={REPL} width="794" height={340 - REPL} fill="url(#subrep)" />

          {/* replacement line */}
          <line
            x1="86"
            x2="880"
            y1={REPL}
            y2={REPL}
            stroke="var(--accent)"
            stroke-width="2.4"
            stroke-dasharray="9 6"
            opacity="0.95"></line>
          <text
            x="878"
            y={REPL - 11}
            fill="var(--accent)"
            font-size="12"
            font-weight="600"
            text-anchor="end"
            font-family="var(--font-mono, monospace)"
            letter-spacing="0.1em">REPLACEMENT · 2.1</text
          >

          {/* axes */}
          {
            yTicks.map((t) => (
